{"title": "Wrong And Still Fine", "type": "Technical lesson", "hooks": ["You can be wrong most of the time and still make money. Here's how.", "Wrong three times out of four, and still roughly even.", "Stop asking how often you win. Ask how much."], "scenes": [{"kind": "hook", "vo": "Stop asking how often you win. Ask how much.", "text": "Wrong most times. Still fine.", "chart": 0, "win": [20, 102], "show": 90}, {"kind": "chart", "chart": 0, "head": "Risk versus reward", "vo": "Compare what you risk with what you aim to make. Say you buy after this dip. The stop goes just under the low.", "cues": [{"say": "after this dip", "do": "mark", "i": 88, "label": "A", "side": "low", "tone": "amber"}, {"say": "just under the low", "do": "line", "price": 92.89, "label": "stop", "tone": "red"}], "win": [20, 102], "show": 90}, {"kind": "chart", "chart": 0, "head": "Target: next resistance", "vo": "The target is the next resistance, the old high at 111.32. Red is the risk, green is the target.", "cues": [{"say": "the old high at 111.32", "do": "line", "price": 111.32, "label": "target", "tone": "green"}], "win": [20, 102], "show": 90}, {"kind": "cards", "head": "One to one, or three", "vo": "Risking one to make one is very different from risking one to make three.", "items": [{"text": "Risk 1, make 1", "sub": "breaks even at half right", "icon": "coin"}, {"text": "Risk 1, make 3", "sub": "room to be wrong more", "icon": "check"}], "cues": [{"say": "risking one to make one", "do": "item", "i": 0}, {"say": "risking one to make three", "do": "item", "i": 1}], "chart": null}, {"kind": "big", "text": "Wrong 3 of 4, still even", "vo": "At one to three, you can be wrong three times out of four and still roughly break even.", "chart": null}, {"kind": "big", "text": "Targets must be realistic", "vo": "But the target has to be realistic, like the next resistance level, not a number you hope for.", "chart": null}, {"kind": "outro", "text": "Plan the trade first", "vo": "Practise planning trades at memestreet.net.", "chart": null}], "caption": "You can be wrong most of the time and still not lose money. Here's how.\nCompare what you risk with what you aim to make.\nRisking 1 to make 3 is very different from risking 1 to make 1.\nAt 1 to 3, you can be wrong three times out of four and still roughly break even.\nBut the target has to be realistic, like the next resistance level.\nSave this before your next trade.\nPractise at memestreet.net\nFictional market. Not investment advice.\n#MemeStreet #RiskReward #RiskManagement #LearnToTrade", "charts": [{"candles": [[89.31, 89.58, 84.99, 87.58, 99946], [87.59, 87.63, 83.93, 87.15, 102082], [87.19, 88.52, 85.96, 86.1, 68970], [86.11, 88.78, 79.98, 83.68, 192167], [83.69, 85.84, 81.43, 84.71, 98483], [84.65, 88.05, 84.32, 87.37, 61863], [87.43, 89.3, 87.34, 87.67, 52962], [87.63, 88.41, 81.72, 83.4, 70149], [83.4, 84.28, 83.03, 83.57, 27678], [83.56, 86.19, 83.32, 86.03, 34680], [86.06, 88.26, 85.78, 88.23, 22452], [88.23, 89.46, 87.72, 89.37, 42218], [89.35, 92.11, 89.35, 91.25, 35375], [91.27, 92.89, 90.62, 91.73, 42810], [91.74, 91.81, 88.78, 89.31, 33747], [89.32, 91.96, 89.04, 90.78, 44501], [90.81, 90.91, 87.15, 89.28, 62997], [89.26, 90.08, 86.38, 88.75, 122127], [88.83, 89.36, 87.54, 87.9, 56235], [87.9, 87.98, 84.86, 86.82, 147248], [86.81, 87.21, 84.8, 85.14, 80010], [85.19, 86.61, 84.19, 85.95, 44920], [85.96, 85.99, 85.29, 85.33, 15326], [85.32, 85.84, 83.24, 83.53, 22659], [83.53, 83.75, 82.38, 83.68, 15938], [83.67, 84.98, 79.61, 81.18, 33470], [81.13, 82.48, 81.13, 82.38, 16848], [82.37, 83.04, 82.37, 82.87, 7496], [82.85, 83.9, 82.83, 83.78, 10665], [83.76, 85.49, 83.76, 85.04, 14444], [85.02, 85.58, 85.02, 85.57, 5770], [85.57, 86.95, 85.12, 85.2, 7579], [85.19, 86.08, 85.02, 86.08, 10628], [86.08, 86.76, 85.51, 86.64, 7979], [86.63, 86.82, 86.5, 86.82, 5570], [86.81, 87.0, 86.81, 86.95, 7244], [86.95, 87.2, 86.93, 87.2, 6245], [87.2, 87.46, 87.15, 87.44, 7312], [87.44, 87.89, 87.44, 87.89, 542